{"type":"message","id":"8046fd44","parentId":"fe56efc8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:02:24.325Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Git push failed because there's no credentials configured for HTTPS. This is likely a known issue. Let me check the backup-fail record and the TOOLS.md to see if there's something about git credentials.\n\nActually, looking at the TOOLS.md, there's no git credentials info. This seems like a recurring issue based on the file `workspace/memory/backup-fail-2026-05-31.md`. Let me check what happened yesterday and if there's a known fix.\n\nLet me read the backup-fail file to understand the context.","thinkingSignature":"65c05c8417bae355b4cbfe4f47d32680df723753330a88757c1f40da2c23927d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_uimvsimc1mrs_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/memory/backup-fail-2026-05-31.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":1040,"output":155,"cacheRead":17241,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18436,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780358540705,"responseId":"066d508d7a898ba45c4f537b93eeca0f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"07080ff4","parentId":"8046fd44","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:02:24.391Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_uimvsimc1mrs_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 备份失败记录\n\n## 时间\n2026-05-31 00:00 UTC (北京时间 08:00)\n\n## 失败原因\n- SSH命令不存在：`error: cannot run ssh: No such file or directory`\n- HTTPS方式需要密码，但没有credential存储\n\n## 已尝试\n1. 原始remote: git@github.com:blocklee/my-openclaw.git (SSH)\n2. 尝试改为HTTPS: fatal: could not read Username for 'https://github.com': terminal prompts disabled\n\n## 影响\n日常备份任务失败，commit已生成本地但未推送到远程\n下次运行时会包含本次commit一起推送\n\n## 建议\n- 安装ssh client\n- 或配置git credential store存储GitHub token\n- 或使用GitHub Personal Access Token替代密码"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780358544385}}
{"type":"message","id":"03b00ce5","parentId":"07080ff4","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:02:30.730Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the issue is known - there's no SSH client and no HTTPS credentials. The git remote is set to SSH (git@github.com:...), but ssh isn't available. When trying HTTPS, there's no credential store.\n\nThis is a recurring backup failure. The boss needs to set up either:\n1. SSH client\n2. GitHub token with credential store\n\nBut since this is a cron job running at midnight and I can't configure credentials myself without potentially exposing them, I should just note the failure and move on. The commit is made locally, so the work isn't lost - it'll be pushed when credentials are available.\n\nLet me just report this quietly. The backup failed due to the same issue as yesterday - no git credentials for push.","thinkingSignature":"18cd60f1199d234e5b1502c2ec1c7de5ff3f4976540db1b0960e8fb1fa83ab13"},{"type":"text","text":"备份失败，原因同昨天：git push 需要 SSH client 或 HTTPS 凭证，但两者都不可用。本地 commit 已生成，远程同步待解决。\n\n建议 boss 配置 GitHub credentials（SSH key 或 PAT + credential store）后可自动恢复。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":1373,"output":201,"cacheRead":17241,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18815,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780358544392,"responseId":"066d50915fa65256534aa5f8258d46b8"}}
